<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#oil-palm">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oil palm</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The oil palm is a tree native to West and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-africa">Central Africa</a> whose fruit yields <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palm-oil">palm oil</a>, an important food and trade product. It was cultivated across the forest and savanna zones of the region. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luba-empire">Luba Empire</a>, oil palm was grown alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sorghum">sorghum</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/millet">millet</a> and yams in the fertile <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upemba-depression">Upemba Depression</a>, supporting dense populations.</p></div>
